From: Alp Lab AB <contact@alplab.ai>
Date: Wed, 4 Jun 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] brcmfmac: sdio: include <uapi/linux/sched/types.h> for 6.1

Copyright (c) 2026 Alp Lab AB
SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0

Backport-shim for building the Murata cyw-fmac backports tree (base
v6.1.97, branch imx-mickledore-jaculus) against a 6.1.141 (cip43) target
kernel.

brcmfmac/sdio.c uses `struct sched_param` (via sched_set_fifo / the
watchdog thread priority setup) but no longer gets the definition pulled
in transitively on 6.1.x: the header reshuffle that moved struct
sched_param into <uapi/linux/sched/types.h> means the bundled sdio.c
fails to compile with an incomplete-type error unless the header is
included explicitly. Add the include next to the other <linux/sched/*>
includes.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [kernel-version backport shim; the Murata
backports tree must include this itself for 6.1.x targets, not the
distro layer]

Signed-off-by: Alp Lab AB <contact@alplab.ai>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/sdio.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/sdio.c b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/sdio.c
index aa26e9a..7948634 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/sdio.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/sdio.c
@@ -13,6 +13,7 @@
 #include <linux/netdevice.h>
 #include <linux/interrupt.h>
 #include <linux/sched/signal.h>
+#include <uapi/linux/sched/types.h>	/* struct sched_param (6.1: no longer pulled in transitively) */
 #include <linux/mmc/sdio.h>
 #include <linux/mmc/sdio_ids.h>
 #include <linux/mmc/sdio_func.h>
--
2.43.0
